Subject: transcript markdown: one parser, link policy, autolinks, lazy math

What: context/marked.tsx is the kit's one markdown parser; upstream's marked-parser.tsx
and marked-theme-register.tsx are removed, and the OpenCode highlight theme stays in
marked-theme.tsx, registered with @pierre/diffs lazily on first highlight. The parser
carries the transcript's extensions: the app's own link schemes autolinked in prose,
only allowed URI schemes rendered as links, raw HTML escaped, math rendered through a
lazily imported module. en.ts gains the strings the transcript renderers read.
Why: sanitization findings P-68, P-69, P-78 and S-2 (markdown, link and mermaid
injection). KaTeX's stylesheet (about 30 KB raw, 21 @font-face rules) no longer loads
in styles/index.css: it ships with the lazy math chunk, not in every eager bundle.

